     c: 'Mao''s comment "On the anti-China question," on the embassy''s report of China''s fair in East Pakistan and the crowds at its pavilion in New Delhi: the "great anti-China" chorus imperialists, reactionaries and revisionists, perhaps 5, at most 10 percent of mankind, and intermittent; when China''s output nears theirs America will have to recognize it and trade.'
