@@ -4580,7 +4653,7 @@ entries:
     date: '1960-03-23'
     thread: china-leadership
     c: 'The Center''s circular, drafted by Mao, forwarding Shandong''s bulletin no. 2 to the county committees: Shandong''s problems are surely in every province, differing little; in some counties and communes the Zhengzhou resolution of last March and the Shanghai conference''s eighteen questions of last April are forgotten, and the "communist wind", exaggeration and commandism are back; some commune staff act without approval; graft, waste and bureaucratism again. The Center believes most communes are good; the worst staff are to be removed, "levelling and transfers" repaid in full, big embezzlers prosecuted, and county committees that failed in their duty removed too; rectification every year, a six-level conference twice a year.'
