@@ -7367,6 +7390,13 @@ entries:
     c: 'Zhejiang 浙江. Chen Yun 陈云, hearing the heads of the Zhejiang committee 中共浙江省委: 1958''s output overestimated; in three years the mess halls, the water-works armies, seed and exports took 20 billion jin more, and the townspeople''s rations alone 16.7 billion jin of rice more; surplus provinces (Heilongjiang 黑龙江, Sichuan 四川, Jiangxi 江西, Zhejiang) send out more and more, the self-sufficient (Anhui 安徽, Hubei 湖北, Guangdong 广东, Guizhou 贵州, Yunnan 云南) and Fujian 福建 must now send out, Henan 河南 too, and Peking 北京, Tianjin 天津, Shanghai 上海 and Liaoning 辽宁 take far more; this year''s loss to disaster about 36 billion jin; the chief cause 30 million more in the towns and mines: cut the outflow by sending townsmen to the villages, and widen the source by more grain (ten thousand small works of 800 tons, fertilizer native and foreign) and by melons and vegetables mixed with grain; mess-hall rations by the head, the saving the eater''s own.'
     n: '[[w.chen-yun-nianpu-xiuding]], III, 54–55. Made public: 2005 ([[w.chen-yun-wenji]], where the nianpu says it is printed). To check: [[w.chen-yun-wenji]], III. Names: Chen Yun.'
